cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Iowa Flood Compendium, please cite it as below."
title: "Iowa Flood Compendium: a multi-source dataset for evaluating flood experiments and impacts in Iowa (2021-2025)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Fuchtman
    given-names: Corin
    affiliation: "IIHR Hydroscience and Engineering, University of Iowa"
  - family-names: Abdelkader
    given-names: Mohamed
    email: mohamed-abdelkader@uiowa.edu
    affiliation: "IIHR Hydroscience and Engineering, University of Iowa"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CorinFuchtman/IA_Flood_Compendium"
abstract: >-
  Episode-based collection of Iowa flood observations, 2021-2025: NOAA Storm
  Events flood episodes joined with Iowa Flood Center and USGS sensors, MRMS
  rainfall, USGS high water marks, FEMA claims, Iowa Flood Center community
  inundation maps, social vulnerability, and geo-referenced flood impact
  records mined from storm narratives and local news with large language
  models. Built to support flood modeling experiments along the forecasting
  chain, from rainfall input to simulated flows to street-scale inundation
  maps and their associated impacts.
keywords:
  - flood
  - Iowa
  - impact-based forecasting
  - flood inundation mapping
  - model evaluation
  - crowdsourcing
license: MIT
